course: dictionary
lesson: 1341
title: Campaign: a planned effort
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A campaign is a planned effort to get something done. Read the words around it to find out what it means. «Suffragists campaigned for votes for women with petitions, meetings and peaceful marches.» Petitions, meetings and marches are all ways of working hard for one goal, so to campaign means to work hard to get people to support a change.
explain: The word can name a whole effort. «The #KyivNotKiev campaign started in 2018» was a planned effort to get people to switch to a new spelling. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Campaign can also mean a series of battles in a war, or a set of adverts to sell something. The clues tell you which one. «Campaign adverts are paid for by the candidate» is about an election, not a battle.
fact: A campaign is a planned series of actions to get something done.
fact: To campaign means to work hard to get people to support something or to make a change.
fact: «Campaigned» is the past tense: «Workers campaigned for weekends.»
fact: A military campaign is a series of battles in one war or area.
fact: An advertising campaign is a set of adverts to sell something.
exercise: «Suffragists campaigned for votes for women with petitions, meetings and peaceful marches.» What does campaigned mean here? | Ran very fast in a race | Sold things with adverts | Fought a battle in a war | *Worked hard to get people to support a change
exercise: In «a nine-year-old boy in Germany starting a tree campaign», what does campaign mean? | A kind of bird | A tall tree | *A planned effort to get something done | A long walk
exercise: What is an advertising campaign? | A list of rules for a school | *A set of adverts to sell something | A small cheap meal | A planned walk in the hills
test: Pupils run a campaign to stop litter. What does run a campaign mean? | Clean up one piece of litter | Race around the playground | Write a poem about the sea | *Organise a planned effort to get something done
test: Which is the past tense of campaign? | Campaigner | Campaigning | *Campaigned | Campaigns
exam: «Workers campaigned for weekends.» What does campaigned mean here? | Bought new clothes | *Worked hard to get a change | Rested at weekends | Fought in a war
